1. (Currently amended) Claim 281: A tool comprising a lamination of at least two layers and at least two adhesive layers, the tool comprising:
first and second layers;
a first adhesive layer configured to be cured on the first layer;
a second adhesive layer configured to be cured on the second layer;
the first adhesive layer and the second adhesive layer configured to be cured to each other;
the tool has a circular shape and includes a plurality of arc-shaped cutting segments having an inner arc shape and an outer arc shape, wherein the inner arc shape of each of the arc-shaped cutting segments is directly affixed to an outer perimeter of the first and second layers;
a medial section, wherein the first adhesive layer and the second adhesive layer are located on opposite sides of the medial section and the first layer and the second layer are aligned with the first adhesive layer and the second adhesive layer;
an additional adhesive layer __positioned between the medial section and at least one of the first or second layers__.

2. (Currently amended) Claim 282: The tool of claim 281 wherein the medial section comprises a metal __selected from the group consisting of steel, aluminum, and titanium__.

3. (Currently amended) Claim 283: The tool of claim 282 wherein the metal is a honeycomb structure __having a density of less than 0.1 g/cm³__.

4. (Currently amended) Claim 284: The tool of claim 282 wherein the medial section is a composite material __comprising the metal bonded to a reinforcing material__.

5. (Currently amended) Claim 285: The tool of claim 281 further comprising:
a weld ring at least partially interposed between the perimeter of the first and second layers;
wherein the weld ring is bonded to the medial section;
wherein the plurality of cutting segments are also welded to an outer perimeter of the weld ring;
wherein the weld ring is continuous __and formed from a material different from the first and second layers__.

6. (Currently amended) Claim 286: The tool of claim 285 wherein the weld ring __is formed from a steel material__.

7. (Currently amended) Claim 287: The tool of claim 285 wherein the weld ring __has a thickness between 0.5 mm and 5 mm__.

8. (Currently amended) Claim 288: The tool of claim 285 wherein the weld ring __is welded to the medial section using a friction welding process__.

9. (Original) Claim 290: The tool of claim 285 further comprising an inner ring, wherein the medial section is coupled on an inner perimeter to the inner ring, wherein the inner ring includes a central opening for accommodating a drive shaft.

10. (Currently amended) Claim 291: The tool of claim 290 wherein the inner ring __is formed from a material selected from the group consisting of steel, aluminum, and composite materials__.

11. (Currently amended) Claim 293: The tool of claim 281 further comprising:
a weld ring at least partially interposed between the perimeter of the first and second layers and the plurality of cutting segments, such that the plurality of cutting segments are located on an outer periphery of the weld ring;
wherein the weld ring is continuous __and has a radial thickness that varies around its circumference__.

12. (Currently amended) Claim 294: The tool of claim 293 wherein the weld ring __is bonded to the medial section using an adhesive layer__.
